    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d890">

                <pb facs="1184" n="1170" xml:id="pg1170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.0146/9–2044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-20T02:00:00+07:00">September 20,
                            1944—2 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1587. Civil administration of liberated areas. Department’s 1219, September 16
                    crossed our 1581, September 19. As indicated in latter, Embassy proposes to let
                    matter rest until it receives further anticipated approach by Foreign
                    Office.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
